<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela's Mavesa starts trading ADSs.</title>
<headline>Venezuela's Mavesa starts trading ADSs.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuelan leading foods company Mavesa said its American Depositary Shares (ADS) began trading on the New York Stock Exchange on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Each ADS represents 20 shares of common stock and appears under the symbol MAV.N, the company said in a release.</p>
<p>It said it accepted for exchange a total 6.16 million Rule 144-A ADS and that 218,122 will remain outstanding.</p>
<p>Mavesa Chairman Jonathan Coles said, according to the statement, that &quot;listing on the NYSE will provide our company with increased trading liquidity and will enhance the presence of Mavesa in the investment community.&quot;</p>
<p>((-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
